<Slide style={{ width: 1280, height: 720, background: '#0A1020', fontFamily: 'Arial', padding: '52px 60px 30px 60px', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column' }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#4D8DFF', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 2.2 }}>05 · HYPOTHESES</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 36, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', lineHeight: 1.2, marginTop: 8 }}>
        Four hypotheses, criteria fixed before the first run
    </Text>
    <Box style={{ width: 1160, height: 1, background: '#24334C', marginTop: 14 }} />

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'column', width: 1128, marginTop: 20 }}>
        <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', background: '#16233A', padding: '9px 16px' }}>
            <Text style={{ width: 56, fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF' }} />
            <Text style={{ width: 448, fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF' }}>Hypothesis</Text>
            <Text style={{ width: 132, fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF' }}>Benchmark</Text>
            <Text style={{ width: 492, fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF' }}>Refuted if — operational criterion</Text>
        </Box>
        {[
            ['H1', 'Λ orders the same way as the tiers', 'PolyBench', 'Spearman ρ < 0.5, or any inversion spanning ≥ 2 tiers'],
            ['H2', 'A tenfold increase in data cannot halve Λ', 'PB26', 'Slope κ significantly < 0 AND Λ at the largest n is below half of Λ at the smallest n'],
            ['H3', 'The gain comes from chain input, not the model', 'OpenPoly', 'Proposal: “the architecture swap yields the larger reduction”. Never tested — A5 has no target'],
            ['H4', 'n* tracks label noise, not sample size', 'OpenPoly', 'Proposal: n* must vary with label dispersion rather than with n. Descriptive here — no test defined'],
        ].map(([tag, claim, bench, rule]) => (
            <Box key={tag} style={{ flexDirection: 'row', padding: '9px 16px', background: '#0E1728', borderBottom: '1px solid #1D2A40' }}>
                <Text style={{ width: 56, fontSize: 19, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#4D8DFF' }}>{tag}</Text>
                <Text style={{ width: 448, fontSize: 18, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', lineHeight: 1.3 }}>{claim}</Text>
                <Text style={{ width: 132, fontSize: 17, color: '#C3D0E2' }}>{bench}</Text>
                <Text style={{ width: 492, fontSize: 18, color: '#C3D0E2', lineHeight: 1.3 }}>{rule}</Text>
            </Box>
        ))}
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', gap: 40, marginTop: 22 }}>
        <Box style={{ width: 640, flexDirection: 'column', gap: 6 }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 18, color: '#FFFFFF', lineHeight: 1.45 }}>
                H1 and H2 are quoted from the proposal (v1.3); H3 and H4 carry their own criterion and their actual status.
            </Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#A8B8CE', lineHeight: 1.4 }}>
                H3 never became runnable — A5 has no labelled target. H4 compares crossings across properties, which three
                properties cannot support. So: H3 untested, H4 descriptive, and no criterion moved after the numbers arrived.
            </Text>
        </Box>
        <Box style={{ width: 470, flexDirection: 'column', gap: 5 }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 16, color: '#FFB020', lineHeight: 1.45 }}>
                <span style={{ fontWeight: 'bold' }}>H2′ is not on this list.</span> It reads the same claim on the absolute gain:
                <span style={{ fontStyle: 'italic' }}> a tenfold increase cannot halve ΔR²</span> (slide 12).
            </Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 15, color: '#A8B8CE', lineHeight: 1.45 }}>
                Stated after the numbers, reported beside H2, never merged into its verdict.
            </Text>
        </Box>
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', justifyContent: 'space-between', marginTop: 'auto' }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#8FA3BC' }}>Group 32 · How Much Is a Chain Worth?</Text>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#8FA3BC' }}>6 / 18</Text>
    </Box>
</Slide>
